{"nodes": [{"id": "claude_md_doc", "label": "CLAUDE.md \u2014 root canon for the repo: repo layout, session entry point, the graphify navigation graph, the hard rules, and the artefact-arm summary.", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_repo_layout_v3_canon", "label": "Repo layout: v3/ is the work \u2014 a lean self-contained HERB evaluation harness with three arms (artefact / lucene / vector) scored with RAGAS, design reference v3/README.md; root canon (CLAUDE.md, README.md) plus the gitignored docs/ state/handoff docs complete the picture.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_session_entry_state_docs", "label": "Session entry point: work continues across sessions via state-transfer documents in docs/state/ (gitignored, never committed, so a fresh clone starts empty); read the current entry doc 2026-06-25-v3-vector-eval-k-vs-topk-ragas-ops.md first, newest dated doc is the entry, with v3/README.md, MEMORY.md, and frozen docs/handoff/ behind it.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_graphify_nav_graph", "label": "The graphify navigation graph (graphify-out/graph.json) covers v3/ plus the in-repo state/handoff docs plus root canon wired by bridge edges; query it FIRST before grepping with graphify query / explain / path.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_refresh_graph_procedure", "label": "After changing files run python refresh_graph.py (repo root) as the ONLY rebuild path \u2014 never graphify --update (it drops the external-doc bridges); if it prints a worklist, extract each listed doc bridging into existing concepts, write repo docs to the semantic cache and state/handoff docs as sidecar fragments in graphify-out/.external_cache/, then re-run.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_hard_rules", "label": "The Hard rules section: design-before-build sign-off gate, plain-English short answers, heed user intent never correct it with stale context, docs track reality by removal not banners, no historical/defensive comments, always refresh the graph after edits, critical-review code you write.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_design_before_build", "label": "Design before build: no pipeline code until the relevant stage's design is explicitly signed off by the user; present decided-vs-open and get the sign-off.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_plain_english_short_answers", "label": "Talk to the user in plain spoken English with short answers \u2014 no jargon walls, no spec-sheet dumps \u2014 and verify claims against the real system/data before asserting.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_heed_user_intent", "label": "Heed the user's intent, never correct it with stale context: when the user names something they want it is the spec, build to it; don't use older notes to argue a current requirement away \u2014 surface a genuine conflict as a question, not a correction.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_docs_track_reality", "label": "Docs track reality: when a decision closes, update the design doc plus memory in the same pass by removal of dead content, not banners; dated state/handoff docs are frozen and describe that moment.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_no_historical_comments", "label": "No historical or defensive comments: code, docs and commit messages state only the present as if written correctly the first time \u2014 never narrate a past mistake, change, or review finding ('previously/now', 'no longer', 'NOT because', review-finding labels) because comments feed the graph and memory and scar tissue pollutes every future session.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_always_refresh_graph", "label": "Always refresh the navigation graph after changing files: after any edit to v3/, root canon, or the external state/handoff docs run python refresh_graph.py \u2014 the ONLY rebuild path \u2014 and process any worklist it prints before the change is done.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_critical_review_code", "label": "Critical-review the code you write: after writing or changing code in v3/, before reporting the work done, run /critical-review on the changed files (it spawns the read-only critical-reviewer) and resolve its findings until the code converges; skip only for trivial non-logic edits.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_artefact_arm_native", "label": "The artefact arm is the system under test, rebuilt natively in v3/artefact/: deterministic tested stages exist (scan.py, probe.py, derive_corpus.py, resolver_prototype.py) with the HERB mapping key and DESIGN/MODEL_CONTRACTS, and the graph proper (chunk \u2192 tag \u2192 facet retrieval) driven by pipelines/artifact.py is the unbuilt part.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_graph_spine_closed_canon", "label": "The graph spine is closed canon: Source \u2192 File \u2192 Chunk \u2192 Tag are the only nodes, hard fields are chunk attributes, and the graph is references into untouched raw source never copies \u2014 never put values, inventories, or mirrors of metadata directories into it.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_model_emits_no_numbers", "label": "The model emits no numbers, ever (tagger and interpreter); the chunk description is dead and tags are per-chunk contextual phrases.", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_md_herb_eval_baseline_only", "label": "herb-eval (Neo4j) is the prior artefact build under the superseded design \u2014 a contrast/forensic baseline only, not adopted; the v3 artefact rebuilds from raw natively in v3/artefact/ and never query herb (oracle-contaminated).", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "claude_md_repo_layout_v3_canon", "target": "claude_md_doc", "relation": "references", "confidence"